# {{lb|en|mobile telephony}} [[Internet]] data transfer over a [[cellular]] telephone [[network]] rather than [[Wi-Fi]].
#: {{syn|en|data|id1=telephony}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|url=http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2010/jun/11/mobile-data-unlimited-end|title=Why file-sharing has killed 'unlimited' mobile data contracts|date=2010-06-11|author=Charles Arthur|passage=Yet O2 says that while it has doubled the number of iPhone users, '''mobile data''' use is doubling every 4 months, equivalent to an eightfold growth every year.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261025185208/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2010/jun/11/mobile-data-unlimited-end|archivedate=25 October 2026}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|url=http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/mar/05/uk-among-countries-with-priciest-mobile-data-plans-in-europe|title=UK among countries with priciest mobile data plans in Europe|date=2019-03-05|author=Rupert Jones|passage=The analysis of '''mobile data''' plans in 230 countries revealed that the UK ranked a “disappointing” 136th when the cost of one gigabyte (1GB) of '''mobile data''' was looked at.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261025185218/https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/mar/05/uk-among-countries-with-priciest-mobile-data-plans-in-europe|archivedate=25 October 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.computerworld.com/article/3379616/why-you-should-stop-using-mobile-data.html|title=Why you should stop using mobile data|date=2019-03-23|author=Mike Elgan|work=Computerworld|passage=By turning off '''mobile data''', you end up with a dumb or minimalist phone while out and about, but a fully internet-connected smartphone while at home, at work and in coffee shops and restaurants that provide Wi-Fi.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231201193240/https://www.computerworld.com/article/3379616/why-you-should-stop-using-mobile-data.html|archivedate=1 December 2023}}

